Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) — scope note

CC BY 4.0 applies to: the query lists, schemas, provenance/methodology documents, annotations,
evaluation labels, manifests, and code authored by Curify for this repository (everything under
`data/*/queries.csv`, `data/*/evaluations.csv`, `data/*/automated_relevance_labels.csv`,
`data/*/schema.json`, `data/*/provenance.json`, `data/*/results.jsonl`,
`data/*/image_manifest.json`, all `.md` documentation, and the gallery/scripts code). You are free
to share and adapt that material for any purpose, even commercially, as long as you give
appropriate credit to Curify (https://curify-ai.com) and indicate if changes were made.

**CC BY 4.0 does NOT apply to the third-party screenshot images in `data/68-query/images/` or
`data/326-query/google-images/`.** The 62 files in `data/68-query/images/` are screenshots of
search-result pages from Bing, Google, Canva, and Pinterest (plus Curify's own product); the 326
files in `data/326-query/google-images/` are Google Images search-result screenshots. Both are
included solely as benchmark evidence under a fair-use/evaluation rationale. Copyright in the
underlying page designs, product photography, and any depicted content remains with its original
rights holders (the respective platforms and/or the creators of the depicted content) — it is not
relicensed, and this repository does not grant any license to reuse, retrain on, resell, or
redistribute those images outside of citing/discussing this benchmark. See
`docs/IMAGE_RIGHTS_AND_ATTRIBUTION_REVIEW.md` for the full rationale and limitations. The 326
Curify screenshots in `data/326-query/curify/` are Curify's own product UI and content, and remain
under the general CC BY 4.0 terms above like the Curify screenshots in `data/68-query/images/`.

